detail_route.tcl records the antenna diode count with utl::metric_int,
which is not a command: the command is utl::metric_integer, and the
short name resolved only through OpenSTA's global unknown handler, which
tries an unknown name as an abbreviation.  With that handler scoped to
read_sdc (patches/0003-opensta-read-sdc-scoped-unknown.patch) the route
stage of a design that skips detailed routing fails with
invalid command name "utl::metric_int".

Spell it out.  This is the only abbreviated command in flow/scripts,
flow/platforms and flow/util: every command token there was checked
against the command set of the built openroad binary.

Submitted upstream as ORFS PR #4542.  Retires on a //:bump onto an
ORFS carrying it.

diff --git a/flow/scripts/detail_route.tcl b/flow/scripts/detail_route.tcl
index 907f4b708..538e8476e 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/detail_route.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/detail_route.tcl
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@ if { !$::env(SKIP_DETAILED_ROUTE) } {
       incr repair_antennas_iters
     }
   } else {
-    utl::metric_int "antenna_diodes_count" -1
+    utl::metric_integer "antenna_diodes_count" -1
   }
 
   source_step_tcl POST DETAIL_ROUTE
